<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <title>Connect to your Solidus store</title>
    <%= stylesheet_link_tag "solidus_mcp/admin", "solidus_mcp/consent" %>
  </head>
  <body class="solidus-mcp-consent">
    <main class="solidus-mcp-admin solidus-mcp-consent-card" aria-labelledby="consent-heading">
      <header>
        <h1 id="consent-heading" class="solidus-mcp-page-title">Connect <%= @pre_auth.client.application.name %> to your Solidus store</h1>
        <p>Only authorize an application you intended to connect. If someone sent you this link unexpectedly, deny the request.</p>
        <p class="solidus-mcp-consent-address"><strong>Return address:</strong> <%= @pre_auth.redirect_uri %></p>
      </header>
      <div class="solidus-mcp-consent-access">
        <% if @pre_auth.scopes.include?("mcp:read") %>
          <section class="solidus-mcp-consent-scope">
            <h2>Read access</h2>
            <ul><li>Search products and variants.</li><li>View prices and inventory.</li><li>Read order information.</li></ul>
          </section>
        <% end %>
        <% if @pre_auth.scopes.include?("mcp:write") %>
          <section class="solidus-mcp-consent-scope">
            <h2>Write access</h2>
            <ul><li>Modify product information.</li><li>Update prices.</li><li>Perform other explicitly enabled store-management operations.</li></ul>
          </section>
        <% end %>
      </div>
      <p>Administrators must also enable individual tools in AI connections. They can change enabled tools within this access level without reconnecting.</p>
      <div class="solidus-mcp-consent-actions">
        <% {"Authorize" => :post, "Deny" => :delete}.each do |label, method| %>
          <%= form_tag "#{SolidusMcp.configuration.endpoint_url}/oauth/authorize", method: method do %>
            <% %i[client_id redirect_uri state response_type scope code_challenge code_challenge_method resource].each do |key| %>
              <%= hidden_field_tag key, params[key], id: nil %>
            <% end %>
            <%= submit_tag label, class: "solidus-mcp-button#{' solidus-mcp-button-primary' if method == :post}" %>
          <% end %>
        <% end %>
      </div>
      <details class="solidus-mcp-consent-review">
        <summary>Change requested access</summary>
        <p>Need to use write tools? You can change the access requested for this connection. You’ll review your selection before approving.</p>
        <%= form_tag "#{SolidusMcp.configuration.endpoint_url}/oauth/authorize", method: :get, id: "review-oauth-scopes" do %>
          <%= hidden_field_tag :review_scopes, "1" %>
          <% %i[client_id redirect_uri state response_type code_challenge code_challenge_method resource].each do |key| %>
            <%= hidden_field_tag key, params[key], id: nil %>
          <% end %>
          <% scope_options.each do |scope| %>
            <p><label class="solidus-mcp-consent-choice">
              <%= check_box_tag "requested_scopes[]", scope, @pre_auth.scopes.include?(scope), id: "oauth_scope_#{scope.tr(':', '_')}" %>
              <span><%= scope == "mcp:write" ? "Use enabled write tools, including tools enabled later" : "Use enabled read tools" %> (<code><%= scope %></code>)</span>
            </label></p>
          <% end %>
          <%= submit_tag "Review access", class: "solidus-mcp-button" %>
        <% end %>
        <p>Read and write access are separate; select both if you need both. Individual tools must still be enabled in AI connections. If write access is not listed, the client's registration must be updated before reconnecting.</p>
      </details>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
